WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Let's see how to deploy an ASP.NET app on Google Compute Engine

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.700
Go to Cloud Launcher and search for ASP.NET

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.700
Click on Launch on Compute Engine

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.700
Give your deployment a name, select the zone

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.700
And click deploy. This will deploy Windows Server

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.700
IIS, SQL Express, and ASP.NET on Compute Engine instance

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.700
Once deployed, go to Compute Engine instance

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.700
And create a Windows user and password

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.700
Note down the password

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.700
Also, note down the external IP

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.700
of the instance. Go to Visual Studio

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.700
where we have a simple HelloWorld ASP.NET app

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.700
Right click on the project, select publish and create a custom profile

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.700
Enter external IP as server and destination URL

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.700
Give a site name, enter Windows username and password

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.700
And validate connection. Finally, select "Remove additional files at destination"

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.700
Hit Publish. Once Visual Studio is done

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.700
your ASP.NET app is published to Google Cloud Compute Engine

